.TH SITECHECK 1 "November 2026" "sitecheck 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sitecheck \- diagnose website availability, DNS resolution, HTTP status codes, and response times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sitecheck
[\fB\-dns\fR \fIDNS_IP\fR]
\fIURL\fR
.br
.B sitecheck
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sitecheck
checks the availability and response behavior of an HTTP or HTTPS URL using base macOS networking tools (\fBcurl\fR and \fBdig\fR).
It supports resolving hostnames via either the system DNS resolver or a custom IPv4 DNS resolver while preserving HTTPS SNI and certificate verification via \fBcurl \-\-resolve\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-dns ", " \-\-dns " " \fIDNS_IP\fR
Resolve the URL hostname using the specified IPv4 DNS server (for example \fB1.1.1.1\fR, \fB8.8.8.8\fR, or \fB9.9.9.9\fR) before connecting.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sitecheck https://github.com
sitecheck https://citizenx.com
sitecheck -dns 1.1.1.1 https://citizenx.com
sitecheck -dns 8.8.8.8 https://citizenx.com
sitecheck -dns 9.9.9.9 https://citizenx.com
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns \fB0\fR on HTTP 2xx/3xx responses (or \fB\-\-help\fR), and \fB1\fR on invalid input, DNS failure, connection failure, or HTTP 4xx/5xx error responses.

